1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
This entire forest is actually one tree.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:03,660
Every single trunk.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,284
It's called Pando, a quaking aspen in

4
00:00:06,284 --> 00:00:08,507
Utah, and every trunk grows from one

5
00:00:08,507 --> 00:00:09,680
shared root system.

6
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,893
That's about 47,000 trunks, all

7
00:00:11,893 --> 00:00:13,180
genetically identical.

8
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:16,349
But here's the wild part: together, it

9
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,120
weighs about 6,000 tonnes.

10
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:19,734
That may make it the heaviest living thing

11
00:00:19,734 --> 00:00:20,080
on Earth.

12
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,120
Its age?

13
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:23,380
Many articles said 80,000 years.

14
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,580
That's now considered way too old.

15
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:29,007
Newer estimates say thousands of years,

16
00:00:29,007 --> 00:00:30,940
maybe 9,000 to 16,000.

17
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,180
But Pando is in trouble.

18
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:33,140
It's shrinking.

19
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,781
Deer and elk eat the young shoots before

20
00:00:35,781 --> 00:00:37,503
they can grow, so old trunks die with

21
00:00:37,503 --> 00:00:38,620
nothing to replace them.

22
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,560
Fences now protect most of it...

23
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,220
but some deer just jump over.

24
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:43,660
Subscribe for more.

